@startuml uc-validate-configuration
!include _theme.iuml

state validateConfiguration as "validateConfiguration()" {

  state " " as RequestingCheck
  state " " as Composing
  state " " as Reporting

  [*] --> RequestingCheck
  note on link
  <b>Policy author</b> asks whether a configuration file is valid
  end note

  RequestingCheck --> Composing
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> loads the document exactly as a GitHub-facing
  command would, and needs no token to do it
  • follows imports relative to the declaring file
  • folds in named policies
  • applies precedence between layers
  end note

  Composing --> Reporting
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> checks every rule that does not need GitHub
  • unknown key, naming the closest declared one
  • value of the wrong kind
  • import or policy cycle, with the chain
  • reference to a policy that was never declared
  • value shaped like an issued credential
  • owner that is not a GitHub account login
  end note

  Reporting --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Policy author</b> reads the resolved owners, or the first
  error with its file and YAML path
  end note
}

validateConfiguration --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
the document is valid; exit 0
end note

validateConfiguration -[#A78BFA]-> NO_CONFIGURATION
note on link
the document does not load; exit 2
end note
@enduml
